--------------------------------------------------------------------------
COPYRIGHT LINE — DELIBERATELY NOT FILLED IN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

An Apache-2.0 NOTICE conventionally opens with a copyright line naming the
holder. That line is absent here on purpose, not by oversight:

  - The repository's LICENSE file carries the Apache License text with its
    unmodified appendix, whose holder field still reads the template value
    `Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]`. The repository therefore
    does not yet state who the copyright holder is.
  - Inventing one here would make this file assert something no other file
    in this repository supports. A NOTICE that names a holder the project
    has never declared is worse than a NOTICE that says the field is open.

Filling this in is an operator decision, not a generated value. Once the
holder is settled, add the line here and in the LICENSE appendix together,
so the two never disagree.

